// READ THIS BEFORE THE SCOPE NOTE BELOW. THIS FILE DOES NOT RUN ON THE REQUIRED GATE, AND THE
// REASON IS NO LONGER THE ONE THIS NOTE USED TO GIVE. It said the required floor DECLINES every
// ReadsLiveTree module (v2.workflow.required_floor DeclinedLiveTree). That arm was DELETED at the
// root of v2.workflow.required_floor, so the reason stated here was true when written and is stale;
// the declaration itself stays, truthfully -- compile_dag_diagnostic_census resolves its synthetic
// sources against the live checkout -- and live_tree_disposition now answers only affected-set
// eligibility.
//
// WHAT IS TRUE TODAY: this module's name matches no row of v2.workflow.required_floor
// required_gate_prefixes and no row of required_gate_authored_modules, so after the 2026-09-19
// nominal-roster ruling the required floor discovers it and dispositions every identity in it
// DeclinedOutsideRequiredGate. A required floor run's green is evidence only for what it PLANNED,
// and nothing here is planned, so every probe below is AUTHORED evidence -- green under a local
// gunbc run --claim-run and under changed-witness selection on a PR that edits it, and executing
// nowhere else. That is strictly weaker than enrolment, and the gap-analysis rows this file serves
// must say so in line. In this file of all files the distinction matters: a witness that cannot
// execute is exactly the defect these probes count, and it applies to them first.
//
// DISSOLVES when a required-gate selector admits this module -- the derived changed-population
// selection v2.workflow.required_floor names as required_gate_bankruptcy's restoration trigger, or
// a re-homing of a class onto an admitted prefix as the zero-field family took (see the note where
// those four sources used to sit). Do NOT dissolve it by relabelling this file SubstrateInputsOnly,
// and do NOT dissolve it by adding a row to either gate roster: that roster is closed to growth
// without operator sign-off.

data guarantee_floor_class_probe_scope_note: String = "WHAT THIS FILE IS. Five floor classes in docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md carried rungs established by a ONE-OFF hand execution of compile_dag_diagnostic_census on 2026-08-01 (four of them said NOT ENROLLED in their own Evidence cell; the parse-separator row cited a session's throwaway probe). A SIXTH class was authored here and REMOVED before merge: the v2.-module direct-call argument-type exemption, which gunbc#8902 landed on main as direct_call_argument_type_class while this change was in flight. One concept, one authority (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority) — that seam is theirs, this file carries no second name for it, and the gap-analysis row for it cites their rows. Nothing re-ran any of them, so each rung was honest about the day it was measured and silent about today -- the shape gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder meta-obligation 4 forbids. This file is the authorship: each of those measurements is written as a probe that reds if the compiler's behaviour changes in either direction. WHERE EACH ONE EXECUTES IS A SEPARATE FACT AND IS NOT UNIFORM -- this module is outside v2.workflow.required_floor required_gate_prefixes and required_gate_authored_modules, so the probes that remain here execute only locally and under changed-witness selection, while the record-completeness ZERO-FIELD family was re-homed onto the admitted test.claim.infer_ prefix at test.claim.infer_record_field_completeness_zero_field_witness and executes on every required floor run. An earlier cut of this sentence claimed required-floor execution for all of them; that was true of the DeclinedLiveTree deletion and false of the roster cut that followed it. Rows that remain holes are ExpectSilentAcceptanceHole (gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus guarantee_probe_below_floor_hole_rows), not a count in this sentence: a hole that climbs is rewritten as ExpectBlockingRefusal and stays as a permanent regression control (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (dissolution on climb)) — floor_field_through_generics_hole_probe / floor_field_through_generics_type_variable_refuses is that climb. Do not read a remaining hole-probe green as a guarantee: it pins a DEFECT. PROBE ADEQUACY, per the operator-adopted 2026-08-01 mandate that every below-floor row carry closure AND shape evidence: each hole ships beside a control that DOES refuse on this same harness and this same run -- the monomorphic record for generic instantiation, the declared-record field access for field-through-generics, the doubled separator for the omitted one, so a zero on the hole is the compiler's silence and never the harness failing to reach the judgment. The exhaustiveness hole's adequacy control is not re-authored here: the coproduct-scrutinee arm is already enrolled and executing at test.claim.match_exhaustiveness_coproduct_witness w_missing_coproduct_arm_reports_one_non_exhaustive, on this same harness, and duplicating it would be a second authority for one fact."

// THE INSTRUMENT THAT PRODUCED EVERY NUMBER BELOW IS A LOCALLY BUILT gunbc, AND ITS VINTAGE WAS
// TESTED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Because the gate does not admit this file (see above), CI never re-runs
// these probes; a single local binary is their ONLY execution evidence, so that binary is a
// variable, not a given. CROSS-CHECK, 2026-08-22: two independently built binaries roughly fifteen
// hours apart ran the same four probes — both silent holes and both refusing controls — and
// returned identical verdicts, PASS on all eight. The pairs stay DISCRIMINATING in both, which is
// what matters: a binary refusing everything or nothing would show as a control flipping, and
// neither did. So the verdicts are not an artifact of one build. NOT established: that any binary
// in this family agrees with the seed CI would use, because no required lane executes this file;
// that question dissolves with gate admission and not before.

// MEASURED 2026-08-22 on this harness, full dag + src/v2 pool, before these probes were authored —
// the numbers the rows below encode. generic-instantiation hole 0 rows; monomorphic control 1
// blocking TypeMismatch; generic green 0. field-through-generics hole 0 rows; declared-record
// control 1 blocking InternalError; green 0. exhaustiveness type-variable hole 0 rows. record
// completeness red 1 blocking MissingField; green 0. parse list separator hole 0 rows;
// doubled-separator control 1 blocking ParseError; green 0. THE InternalError ROW IS PINNED AS
// OBSERVED, NOT AS ENDORSED: a field access naming no declared field refuses, the property the
// control exists to establish, but under a class name that says nothing about what went wrong. That
// is its own diagnostic-quality defect, recorded here rather than laundered into a nicer-sounding
// assertion; improving the class reds this probe, the correct place for the conversation.

fn census_of(source: String) -> CompileDiagnosticCensus {
  compile_dag_diagnostic_census(source)
}

fn measured_v1_compile_harness_source() -> NonEmptyStr {
  fold_list(
    xs: v1_compile_harness_source_paths(),
    empty: "guarantee-floor-class-harness-source" as NonEmptyStr,
    cons: fn(acc, path) {
      let read = filesystem_read(path: path)
      concat(
        concat(concat(acc as String, "\n=== "), path as String),
        concat(" ===\n", read.content as String),
      ) as NonEmptyStr
    },
  )
}

fn witness_harness_revision(probe: GuaranteeProbeId) -> MeasurementRevision {
  let harness_source = measured_v1_compile_harness_source()
  match active_probe_row(probe: probe) {
    Present { value: row } =>
      v1_compile_harness_revision(
        probe: probe,
        expectation: row.expectation,
        harness_source: harness_source,
      )
    Absent =>
      v1_compile_harness_revision(
        probe: probe,
        expectation: ExpectBlockingRefusal { diagnostic_class: "witness-harness-row-absent" as NonEmptyStr },
        harness_source: harness_source,
      )
  }
}

fn total_row_count_is_zero(census: CompileDiagnosticCensus) -> Bool {
  match census {
    CensusObserved { rows: rows } => count(rows) == 0
    CensusNotRunnable { cause: _ } => false
  }
}

fn row_holds(probe: GuaranteeProbeId, source: String) -> Bool {
  match active_probe_row(probe: probe) {
    Present { value: row } => probe_row_expectation_holds(census: census_of(source: source), row: row)
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn silent_hole_holds(probe: GuaranteeProbeId, source: String) -> Bool {
  let census = census_of(source: source)
  match active_probe_row(probe: probe) {
    Present { value: row } =>
      probe_expectation_is_below_floor_hole(e: row.expectation)
        && probe_row_expectation_holds(census: census, row: row)
        && total_row_count_is_zero(census: census)
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn blocking_verdict(source: String, wanted: String, holds: fn(Int) -> Bool) -> CensusVerdict {
  census_verdict(census: blocking_class_census(source: source, wanted_class: wanted), holds: holds)
}

data generic_instantiation_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_generic_inst\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn f() -> Boxed<Int> { Boxed { inner: \"not an int\" } }\n"
data generic_instantiation_monomorphic_source: String = "module probe_floor_generic_mono\ntype Plain { inner: Int }\nfn f() -> Plain { Plain { inner: \"not an int\" } }\n"
data generic_instantiation_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_generic_green\ntype Boxed<T> { inner: T }\nfn f() -> Boxed<Int> { Boxed { inner: 1 } }\n"

data field_through_generics_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_generic\nfn get_field<T>(t: T) -> Int { t.no_such_field }\n"
data field_through_generics_record_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_record\ntype Plain { inner: Int }\nfn f(p: Plain) -> Int { p.no_such_field }\n"
data field_through_generics_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_field_green\ntype Plain { inner: Int }\nfn f(p: Plain) -> Int { p.inner }\n"

data exhaustiveness_type_variable_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_exh_tyvar\ntype Colour = Red | Blue\nfn pick<T>(t: T) -> Int { match t { Red => 1 } }\n"

data record_completeness_red_source: String = "module probe_floor_record_missing\ntype Pair { a: Int, b: Int }\nfn f() -> Pair { Pair { a: 1 } }\n"
data record_completeness_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_record_full\ntype Pair { a: Int, b: Int }\nfn f() -> Pair { Pair { a: 1, b: 2 } }\n"
// THE ZERO-FIELD FORMS OF THIS CLASS MOVED OUT, and this note is the pointer rather than a second
// copy of them. The four sources and five witnesses that measure an empty brace pair, a bare name
// and the sanctioned `discriminant` seam now live at
// `test.claim.infer_record_field_completeness_zero_field_witness`, whose module name matches
// the `test.claim.infer_` row of `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` -- so they
// execute on the required floor, which this module does not. What remains here is the
// PARTIAL-OMISSION red and its green control.

data parse_list_separator_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_list_sep\ntype Cell { n: Int }\nfn f() -> List<Cell> { [ Cell { n: 1 }, Cell { n: 2 }  Cell { n: 3 } ] }\n"
data parse_list_separator_double_source: String = "module probe_floor_list_sep_double\ntype Cell { n: Int }\nfn f() -> List<Cell> { [ Cell { n: 1 }, , Cell { n: 3 } ] }\n"
data parse_list_separator_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_list_sep_green\ntype Cell { n: Int }\nfn f() -> List<Cell> { [ Cell { n: 1 }, Cell { n: 2 }, Cell { n: 3 } ] }\n"

// THE OPTIONAL IS A DECLARED FIELD (parent: Level?), not an import: the T? sugar is builtin, so all
// three fixtures stay std-free and their censuses carry ONLY their own rows - the whole-closure row
// set that gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census warns about (importing fixtures never reach a zero total)
// cannot appear. Measured at the released main compiler (release-bins provenance 816396255c99):
// - the hole: reading a field THROUGH an optional-typed field (l.parent.id) is admitted with zero
//   diagnostics, although parent can be absent and absent has no id field;
// - the green: reading the required field (l.id) is accepted - the pair differs on ONE axis (the
//   dot-after-optional projection), so the hole is the projection position, not optionals generally;
// - the call-argument control: the SAME optional value at a direct call argument IS refused with
//   DeclaredTypeNotInhabited, proving the inhabittance check runs and the hole is position-specific.
data cardinality_seam_hole_source: String = "module probe_floor_cs_hole\ntype Level { id: String, parent: Level? }\nfn probe(l: Level) -> String? { l.parent.id }\n"

data cardinality_seam_green_source: String = "module probe_floor_cs_green\ntype Level { id: String, parent: Level? }\nfn probe(l: Level) -> String { l.id }\n"

data cardinality_seam_call_arg_control_source: String = "module probe_floor_cs_callarg\ntype Level { id: String, parent: Level? }\nfn use_level(l: Level) -> String { l.id }\nfn probe(l: Level) -> String { use_level(l: l.parent) }\n"

// CLIMBED: the type-argument hole is closed at b5af75f4d339 (gunbc#9416; red at its parent 107304a57920). The probe was
// `floor_generic_instantiation_is_still_silently_accepted`; per gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (dissolution on
// climb) it is flipped to the refusal and stays enrolled as the permanent regression control for the higher rung.
test fn floor_generic_instantiation_type_argument_refuses() -> ProcessExit {
  census_verdict_all([
    census_premise("the probe row's expectation holds", row_holds(probe: floor_generic_instantiation_hole_probe, source: generic_instantiation_hole_source)),
    blocking_verdict(source: generic_instantiation_hole_source, wanted: "TypeMismatch", holds: fn(n) { n == 1 })
  ])
}

